+#: The cosine a re-embedded point must reach against the vector stored for it.
+#:
+#: Corruption guard, not a space-drift guard: a vector bound to the wrong point
+#: measures 0.24 (unrelated documents) to 0.93 (the sibling route of the same
+#: model), another space measures ≈ -0.03, and dimension/norm are checked
+#: separately beside this comparison. It was 0.999, which encoded "a
+#: deterministic endpoint reproduces its own vector"; the v2 candidate gateway
+#: (qwen3.7-text-embedding-flash) is stochastic — measured 2026-09-21, 30
+#: repeats per text: answers are bimodal (identical or ~0.998), pooled minimum
+#: 0.997556 over ~1.6k repeat pairs, and the noisy mode moved ~0.0013 between
+#: runs. This audit runs per point, so a ~51k-point rebuild reaches the tail of
+#: that distribution: at 0.999 it aborts with "isolated Milvus vector differs
+#: from its bound embedding", which reads like corruption but is the endpoint's
+#: rounding. 0.99 keeps 0.0076 below the lowest repeat ever measured (3x the
+#: observed spread) and 0.06 above the highest measured wrong answer.
+_MIN_VECTOR_COSINE_SIMILARITY = 0.99
